{
  "evidence": "TEXT_E: “strong and stable leadership”; “leave the single market and customs union… control immigration”; “Preserve the Union”; “meet NATO 2%… retain Trident… stronger policing, counter‑terror and cyber”; “The world’s Great Meritocracy” with selective schools, T‑levels and apprenticeships; NHS funding and a new Mental Health Bill; “fairer corporate governance… crack down on tax evasion.” TEXT_D: Second referendum with option to remain; seek single market/customs union membership and unilaterally guarantee EU citizens’ rights; uprate benefits, 1p on income tax for NHS/care, mental health parity; expand refugee resettlement and end indefinite detention; defend HRA/ECHR and expand LGBT+/BAME rights; proportional representation and Lords reform; decriminalise drug possession; oppose fracking and enact five green laws; oppose new grammars.",
  "reasoning": "Because the electorate’s highest priorities are Authority and Loyalty, TEXT_E’s emphasis on strong leadership, national sovereignty via Brexit and immigration control, preserving the Union, defence, policing, and a meritocratic frame aligns with those foundations while still addressing Care, Equality and Proportionality. TEXT_D leans heavily into Care and Equality and internationalism while proposing institutional and cultural liberalisations (PR, drug decriminalisation, EU re‑alignment) that cut against the electorate’s top Authority/Loyalty priorities.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "winner": "TEXT_E"
}
